{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_79","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"file research/palette/preview-{light,dark}.png; PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python -c 'import PIL; print(PIL.__version__)'; cat bench/test/profile.test.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"research/palette/preview-light.png: PNG image data, 1440 x 764, 8-bit/color RGB, non-interlaced\nresearch/palette/preview-dark.png:  PNG image data, 1440 x 764, 8-bit/color RGB, non-interlaced\n/bin/bash: line 1: python: command not found\n// Pure test: profile attribution, self against inclusive, through a source map (review finding 3). A synthetic\n// profile and map with hand-counted samples.\nimport { test } from 'node:test';\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { summarizeProfile, positionMap, decodeVlq } from '../lib/profile-summary.mjs';\n\n// Line 0 of the bundle: columns 0..9 are data/normalize.ts, from column 10 render/svg.ts.\n// Segments: [col 0, source 0, line 0, col 0] = \"AAAA\"; then [col +10, source +1, line 0, col 0] = \"UCAA\".\nconst map = { version: 3, sources: ['../../packages/axylo/src/data/normalize.ts', '../../packages/axylo/src/render/svg.ts'], mappings: 'AAAA,UCAA' };\nconst url = 'http://127.0.0.1:1/A/axylo/axylo.iife.min.js';\nconst cf = (functionName, columnNumber, u = url) => ({ functionName, url: u, lineNumber: 0, columnNumber, scriptId: '1' });\n// root -> normalize (col 2) -> draw (col 12); root -> (garbage collector); root -> (idle); root -> page code\nconst profile = {\n  nodes: [\n    { id: 1, callFrame: cf('(root)', 0, ''), children: [2, 4, 5, 6] },\n    { id: 2, callFrame: cf('normalize', 2), children: [3] },\n    { id: 3, callFrame: cf('paint', 12), children: [] },\n    { id: 4, callFrame: cf('(garbage collector)', 0, ''), children: [] },\n    { id: 5, callFrame: cf('(idle)', 0, ''), children: [] },\n    { id: 6, callFrame: cf('runCreate', 0, 'http://127.0.0.1:1/A/page.js'), children: [] },\n  ],\n  // 1 ms each: paint x2, normalize x1, gc x1, idle x1, page x1\n  samples: [3, 3, 2, 4, 5, 6],\n  timeDeltas: [1000, 1000, 1000, 1000, 1000, 1000],\n};\n\ntest('the VLQ decoder and the position map read the source map', () => {\n  assert.deepEqual(decodeVlq('UCAA'), [10, 1, 0, 0]);\n  const at = positionMap(map);\n  assert.equal(at(0, 2), 'data/normalize.ts');\n  assert.equal(at(0, 12), 'render/svg.ts');\n  assert.equal(at(1, 0), null);\n});\n\ntest('self time goes to the leaf; inclusive time to every stage on the stack', () => {\n  const s = summarizeProfile(profile, { map, build: 'prod' });\n  const self = Object.fromEntries(s.self.map(r => [r.k, r.ms]));\n  const incl = Object.fromEntries(s.inclusive.map(r => [r.k, r.ms]));\n  assert.equal(s.totalMs, 6);\n  assert.equal(s.busyMs, 5);\n  assert.equal(self.draw, 2);\n  assert.equal(self.normalize, 1);\n  assert.equal(self['(garbage collector)'], 1);\n  assert.equal(self['other JavaScript (harness, page, comparison library)'], 1);\n  assert.equal(incl.normalize, 3, 'normalize is on the stack of its own sample and both paint samples');\n  assert.equal(incl.draw, 2);\n  assert.equal(incl['Axylo (any frame)'], 3);\n  assert.match(s.mapping, /source map from the sealed artifact/);\n});\n\ntest('without a map nothing is guessed', () => {\n  const s = summarizeProfile(profile, { map: null, build: 'prod' });\n  assert.equal(Object.fromEntries(s.self.map(r => [r.k, r.ms]))['axylo (unmapped)'], 3);\n  assert.match(s.mapping, /not available/);\n});\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_80","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'createElement|css|react' packages/react/README.md; rg -n 'benchmark|readout' docs/decisions/0004*; nl -ba docs/decisions/0003-default-palette.md | sed -n '190,230p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_80","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'createElement|css|react' packages/react/README.md; rg -n 'benchmark|readout' docs/decisions/0004*; nl -ba docs/decisions/0003-default-palette.md | sed -n '190,230p'\"","aggregated_output":"1:# @axylo/react\n9:npm install axylo @axylo/react\n15:import { Line } from '@axylo/react';\n7:Revision 1 (placed across the reading axis, offset from the pointer, interactive while hovered) was implemented three times and still failed the acceptance tests: because the tooltip's position followed the pointer it moved away when approached, because it took pointer events it stalled the readout or swallowed the click whenever a move landed on it, and it could cover controls and the focus ring. Revision 2 removes the causes instead of tuning distances.\n9:**Problem.** WCAG 1.4.13 requires content shown on hover to stay when the pointer moves onto it. Spec I1 requires the readout to name the datum at the pointer on every move, the tooltip not to cover the active mark, to stay inside the viewport, and to fall back to a fixed readout when it cannot fit. On a line chart the whole plot picks, so anything that takes pointer events inside the plot blocks picking.\n18:5. **Readout mode is decided by layout, not by hover.** When the plot is narrower than 240 CSS px or shorter than 140 CSS px, the figure is in readout mode: a strip of two text lines is reserved under the plot in the layout, and the content that would be in the tooltip is written there as running text (\"x: series value; series value; +N more\"), wrapping to the two lines and ending in \"+N more\" when it does not fit. The strip is part of the figure's flow: it covers nothing and nothing covers it. In readout mode there is no floating tooltip. A pinned datum makes the strip's entries buttons of 24 px height.\n19:6. **When no candidate is valid outside readout mode** (a tooltip taller than the room around a tall stack, for example), rows are dropped from the end and counted in \"+N more\" until a candidate is valid; if none is with one row, the tooltip is placed inside the plot at the candidate that overlaps the box least. This is the only case in which the active mark may be partly covered, and the table still has every value.\n22:Rejected: revision 1; an interactive hovered tooltip with a \"safe triangle\" (still ambiguous when the reading axis and the approach coincide); always using the readout (loses the association between the values and the mark on plots that have room).\n   190\t- **Slot hues moved within each family.** The light red is a coral (hue 18), the dark red a brick (hue 32). That 13.6° shift is the largest.\n   191\t\n   192\t## Reference palettes (measured)\n   193\t\n   194\tThese are read from the installed d3-scale-chromatic 3.1.1 (`research/harness/node_modules`) by `research/palette/references.mjs` and scored with the same code (`research/palette/references.json`). Minima are over the first eight colors.\n   195\t\n   196\t| Scheme | Below 3:1 on white | Min ΔE normal / protan / deutan / tritan (closest slots) |\n   197\t|---|---|---|\n   198\t| schemeTableau10 | 5 of 10 | 0.129 / 0.016 / 0.007 (3–5, red–green) / 0.064 |\n   199\t| schemeObservable10 | 6 of 10 | 0.113 / 0.059 / 0.020 / 0.046 |\n   200\t| schemeCategory10 (D3's default, Plotly's) | 4 of 10 | 0.113 / 0.007 (2–3) / 0.039 / 0.042 |\n   201\t| schemeDark2 | 2 of 8 | 0.099 / 0.018 / 0.017 / 0.049 |\n   202\t| schemeSet1 | 5 of 9 | 0.130 / 0.031 / 0.035 / 0.066 |\n   203\t\n   204\tLibrary defaults as rendered are in R7 (docs/01-landscape.md). That table has eight displayed six-slice rows. Recharts' row uses its documentation's authored colors, the D3 chart is authored, uPlot has no default palette, and ECharts was read from its options. What I took from these: the blue-then-orange opening (Tableau 10, Category 10), a quiet neutral last, and the evidence that the familiar sets put adjacent hues that deuteranopia merges (Tableau 10's red and green at 0.007). The first version also drew on palettes recalled from memory (IBM Carbon, Okabe–Ito, Paul Tol). No arrays for them are installed here, so they are not cited.\n   205\t\n   206\t## Not verified\n   207\t\n   208\t- The browser suites that sample palette colors were not run, because they need `npm run build`.\n   209\t  - `render.browser.test.ts` and `theme.browser.test.ts` read the colors from `palette.ts`, so they should follow; that is inferred.\n   210\t  - `keyboard.browser.test.ts` checks the light focus only, and that token is unchanged.\n   211\t  - Any browser test that checks the dark focus ring's color would see `#e3e8f0` now.\n   212\t- Raster checks cover isolated fills over the background. A 25% area over another 25% area (overlapping areas) is not scored.\n   213\t- The simulation is Machado at severity 1.0 only.\n   214\t- Strokes and fills were measured in headless Chrome 157 on Linux only.\n   215\t- Nobody with a color-vision deficiency has looked at the previews.\n   216\t\n   217\t## Files\n   218\t\n   219\t- `packages/axylo/src/theme/palette.ts`: both series sets and the dark focus token. Exported names and shapes are unchanged.\n   220\t- `packages/axylo/test/theme/palette.test.ts`: constraints 1–6, analytic and in bytes; Chrome fill pixels; the record at written precision; stroke-record validation.\n   221\t- `research/palette/`: `color.mjs`, `fit.mjs`, `anneal.mjs`, `explore.mjs`, `score.mjs`, `raster.mjs`, `strokes.mjs`, `preview.mjs`, `references.mjs`, `configs/`, `palette.json`, `raster.json`, `strokes.json`, `references.json`, `preview.html` and the two PNGs. See the README there.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_81","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'eight|Eight|8 (series|shown)|slice\\\\(0,|MAX_VISIBLE' packages/axylo/src/{view,data,scene,core} docs/02-product-spec.md; nl -ba packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts | sed -n '69,99p;380,449p'; nl -ba packages/axylo/src/dom/figure.ts | sed -n '185,272p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_81","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'eight|Eight|8 (series|shown)|slice\\\\(0,|MAX_VISIBLE' packages/axylo/src/{view,data,scene,core} docs/02-product-spec.md; nl -ba packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts | sed -n '69,99p;380,449p'; nl -ba packages/axylo/src/dom/figure.ts | sed -n '185,272p'\"","aggregated_output":"docs/02-product-spec.md:55:| Donut | Up to eight slices | What share does each part have? | 1.0 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:101:| F8 | Donut: slices keep the given order, start at 12 o'clock and run clockwise. The legend shows every slice's value and percentage as text, in slice order. A zero slice is listed without an arc; a `null` slice is listed as \"No data\". A negative value is AX120 and the chart shows its error state. With more than eight slices that have an arc (a positive value), the seven largest are drawn and the rest of those are grouped as \"Other (n)\", with AX121; zero and `null` slices never count toward the limit and are never grouped, so each stays listed on its own; the table lists every category. Shares are shown with at most one fraction digit. An all-zero donut shows the empty state. | `parts` fixture; one test per case | R7, landscape scoreboard 3.1 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:102:| F9 | Up to eight series, no two share a color. Beyond eight, each series still has a unique combination of color and dash or marker (for bars: color and fill pattern, which gives 32 distinct combinations; beyond 32 bar series combinations repeat), and AX130 is raised. | Tests with 6, 8 and 12 series | R7 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:103:| F10 | Stacks place positive and negative values on their own sides of zero, and the axis covers both totals. The readout's total is the sum when every component has the same sign; when signs are mixed it gives the positive total and the negative total, the two ends the reader sees, not their net. A missing component is drawn with zero height and the stack is marked \"incomplete\" in tooltip, table and announcements. | Property test on stacked geometry; mixed-sign and incomplete fixtures | R5 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:113:| L3 | The chart follows its container with no call from the page, in both directions. With no definite height, the plot is 16:9, clamped between 160 and 480 CSS px tall, and the title, controls and table flow above and below it. A container that starts hidden or zero-sized draws when it gets a size. | Resize 720 → 360 → 720 px; hidden-then-shown test; `height: auto` container is stable over 10 frames | R16, D1 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:124:| I1 | Pointing anywhere in the plot shows what is there, by the picking rule for the chart type (section 3.6), within one frame at the 95th percentile. On line, area and bar the tooltip lists every visible series at the nearest x; a series with no row at that x reads \"No observation\", distinct from \"No data\". The tooltip stays inside the viewport, does not cover the active mark or any control, can itself be hovered, and lists at most eight rows plus \"+N more\". In a plot too small for it (decision 0004: narrower than 240 px or shorter than 140 px) the same content appears as text in a strip reserved under the plot. Escape closes it until the pointer reaches a different datum. | Hover at 20 positions including all four edges; sparse-series fixture; narrow tile with eight series; Escape test | R15 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:141:| A5 | Series are never distinguished by color alone, in any mode. Each line and area carries a shape marker at its last point and at sparse intervals, repeated in the legend and tooltip; under `prefers-contrast: more` or forced colors, lines also differ by dash. Adjacent filled marks (slices, stacked segments) are separated by at least 1 px of background. The default palette has eight colors, each at least 3:1 on the default light and dark backgrounds, with a minimum pairwise OKLab difference of 0.10 (provisional) under normal vision and simulated protanopia, deuteranopia and tritanopia. On any other background, Axylo measures the palette against the resolved background and raises AX141 below 3:1. | Palette script scoring the rendered marks of an eight-series chart in both schemes, repeats included; rendered-pixel checks of separators; a grayscale screenshot in which three crossing lines can be told apart by marker | R7, WCAG 1.4.1, 1.4.11 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:168:| AX121 | Warning | More than eight donut slices | Seven largest plus \"Other (n)\" |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:169:| AX130 | Warning | More than eight series | All series, with dash or marker differences |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:193:| Tooltip content | Every visible series at that x | Same, plus the stack total | Every series in that category | Label, value, percentage | The point's series, x and y; coincident points listed, up to eight |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:197:| Limit that raises a diagnostic | Eight series | Eight series | Eight series | Eight slices | Eight series |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:208:| C3 | It fills its container at any size from 24×16 CSS px up; with no definite height it is 32 px tall. | Size tests |\npackages/axylo/src/scene/index.ts:24:  const { x: left, y: top, width, height } = layout.plot;\npackages/axylo/src/scene/index.ts:26:  const bottom = top + height;\npackages/axylo/src/scene/index.ts:62:      const line = vertical ? rule('reference', paint, low, plot.y, low, plot.y + plot.height)\npackages/axylo/src/scene/index.ts:66:      const box = vertical ? { ...plot, x: low, width: high - low } : { ...plot, y: low, height: high - low };\npackages/axylo/src/scene/index.ts:82:  const { width, height } = layout;\npackages/axylo/src/scene/index.ts:84:    return { width, height, clip: { x: 0, y: 0, width, height }, marks: [] };\npackages/axylo/src/scene/index.ts:89:    return { width, height, clip, marks };\npackages/axylo/src/scene/index.ts:121:  return { width, height, clip, marks: layers.flat() };\npac