{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_109","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'theme.*class|update|size|role' packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts packages/axylo/src/theme/resolve.ts | head -55; rg -n 'r3|Chrome|verify|focus' docs/decisions/0003-default-palette.md | tail -21; git log --oneline -- packages/axylo/src/dom/swatch.ts | head -6\"","aggregated_output":"packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:11: * Detachment is noticed by the observers the chart already has (the resize observer reports a zero box),\npackages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:120:    // a probe set like the labels changes size whenever their font does, and that is a font load (L1).\npackages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:125:    const fontObserver = new win.ResizeObserver(() => {\npackages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:127:      const size = `${box.width}x${box.height}`;\npackages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:128:      if (probeSize !== null && size !== probeSize && controller !== null && root.isConnected) {\npackages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:132:      probeSize = size;\npackages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:137:    const resizeObserver = new win.ResizeObserver(() => {\npackages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:145:      controller.invalidate.resize();\npackages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:147:    cleanup.push(() => resizeObserver.disconnect());\npackages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:204:    resizeObserver.observe(figure.plot);\npackages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:205:    resizeObserver.observe(figure.figure);\n22:**One token changes.** The dark focus token goes from `#79a8ff` to a near-white `#e3e8f0`, which is 14.4:1 on #16181d. The old focus blue sat at OKLab L 0.735, exactly where a dark-mode series blue belongs. With it kept, no dark set I found had a first blue above L 0.55. The exact search with the blue asked for at 0.62 ended at `#3970c2`, L 0.55 (`configs/dark-n2.json`, best within 300 s). The light focus `#1f5fcc` is unchanged; `keyboard.browser.test.ts` hardcodes it. Every other token is unchanged.\n35:| 25% fills on an 8-bit raster, worst neighbours | 0.0590 (review's raster) | 0.063 (Chrome, canvas and SVG) |\n58:- **Bytes.** Values are rounded where an 8-bit image would round them. A simulated color is encoded and rounded to the nearest byte before the OKLab conversion; that is what the simulated rows of the preview PNGs hold. A translucent fill is quantised as a raster would quantise it: alpha at round(α×255), each channel rounded. That reproduces Chrome 157's canvas and SVG fills on white exactly and is within one byte on #16181d. The second variant, alpha at floor(α×255), is what the review's CPU Skia raster did.\n59:- **Chrome.** The fill pixels Chrome actually drew, canvas and SVG (`research/palette/raster.mjs`).\n61:The unit test requires the analytic and the byte forms. It checks the recorded Chrome pixels against the 0.06 limit, and checks that each recorded pixel is within one byte of the model. A stricter margin is the worst case over every byte color within one byte per channel of both fills. It is recorded but not required, because I found no palette that meets it together with the rest (0.054–0.056 is the best I saw; see below).\n75:| 5 | nearest series color to focus / reference / muted | ≥ 0.10 | 0.101 (cyan) / 0.152 (green) / 0.110 (cyan) | 0.138 (cyan) / 0.104 (cyan) / 0.113 (slate) |\n76:| 6 | neighbour fills at 25%: ideal / byte models / Chrome canvas / Chrome SVG | ≥ 0.06 | 0.064 / 0.063 / 0.063 / 0.063 | 0.064 / 0.064 / 0.063 / 0.063 |\n77:| 6 | neighbour fills at 80%: ideal / byte models / Chrome | ≥ 0.06 | 0.201 / 0.202 / 0.202 | 0.179 / 0.179 / 0.179 |\n109:  - focus distance 0.101 (cyan against `#1f5fcc`).\n122:`strokes.mjs` draws each color as a 2 px random-walk polyline in headless Chrome 157 (canvas and SVG, device pixel ratio 1 and 2) and reads the pixels back. For each pixel column it records two values:\n162:3. **Dark against that light set.** The searches with the old focus token failed: `dark-a2.json` (annealing) and `dark-n2.json` (exact; best blue L 0.55). Moving the dark focus to near-white let annealing find a set with a light dark-mode blue and a deeper purple (`configs/dark-c.json`).\n174:- **Magenta fourth instead of purple**, to relieve the dark blue (`configs/mag4-a.json`): feasible on white. Its dark set was proved infeasible with the old focus token (exact search, `configs/dark-n2-m4.json`), and annealing found none with the new one (`configs/dark-b2-m4.json`).\n181:- **Byte-level checks** (tested): byte-rounded simulation; fills on both 8-bit raster models; Chrome's drawn pixels within one byte of the model and 0.06 apart.\n188:- **The dark focus ring becomes near-white `#e3e8f0`** (light stays blue). This is a visible UI change, made to free the dark blue. The alternative is to keep `#79a8ff` and accept a dark blue near L 0.55.\n210:  - `keyboard.browser.test.ts` checks the light focus only, and that token is unchanged.\n211:  - Any browser test that checks the dark focus ring's color would see `#e3e8f0` now.\n214:- Strokes and fills were measured in headless Chrome 157 on Linux only.\n219:- `packages/axylo/src/theme/palette.ts`: both series sets and the dark focus token. Exported names and shapes are unchanged.\n220:- `packages/axylo/test/theme/palette.test.ts`: constraints 1–6, analytic and in bytes; Chrome fill pixels; the record at written precision; stroke-record validation.\n4809516 Chart core: interaction and accessibility review fixes (22 findings) and later reports\n156f414 Chart core: the 20 findings of the first core review fixed; SVG default; legend positions\n5e187a4 Chart core, part 2 (Opus 5.5 high): tooltip, keyboard proxy, toolbar and legend, zoom, pause, table, announcements\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_110","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"node --input-type=module <<'NODE'\n\nimport fs from 'node:fs';\nconst specs={ light:{ series:'#4a94eb #e97200 #136102 #7314a2 #bd585e #007baa #a52265 #9293a5'.split(' '), background:'#ffffff', focus:'#1f5fcc', reference:'#474b55', muted:'#62666f' },\n  dark:{ series:'#64acfa #de7b2e #b2e390 #9149b9 #c3513d #71d8ff #f898b5 #7a7f93'.split(' '),background:'#16181d',focus:'#e3e8f0',reference:'#bcc0c9',muted:'#9da2ad'} };\nconst load=(name)=>JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('research/palette/'+name+'.json','utf8'));\nconst rom=load('palette'), raster=load('raster');\nconst rgbXyz=[[506752/1228815,87881/245763,12673/70218],[87098/409605,175762/245763,12673/175545],[7918/409605,87881/737289,1001167/1053270]];\nconst xyzLms=[[.819022437996703,.3619062600528904,-.1288737815209879],[.0329836539323885,.9292868615863434,.0361446663506424],[.0481771893596242,.2642395317527308,.6335478284694309]];\nconst labLms=[[1,.3963377773761749,.2158037573099136],[1,-.1055613458156586,-.0638541728258133],[1,-.0894841775298119,-1.2914855480194092]];\nconst cvd={\n  normal:[[1,0,0],[0,1,0],[0,0,1]],\n  protan:[[.152286,1.052583,-.204868],[.114503,.786281,.099216],[-.003882,-.048116,1.051998]],\n  deutan:[[.367322,.860646,-.227968],[.280085,.672501,.047413],[-.011820,.042940,.968881]],\n  tritan:[[1.255528,-.076749,-.178779],[-.078411,.930809,.147602],[.004733,.691367,.303900]]\n};\nconst visions=Object.keys(cvd);\nfunction inv(matrix){\n  const m=matrix.map((row,i)=>[...row,...[0,1,2].map(j=>i===j?1:0)]);\n  for(let i=0;i<3;i++){\n    m[i]=m[i].map(x=>x/m[i][i]);\n    for(let j=0;j<3;j++)if(i\"'!==j){const c=m[j][i];m[j]=m[j].map((x,k)=>x-c*m[i][k]);}\n  }\n  return m.map(row=>row.slice(3));\n}\nconst dot=(x,y)=>x.reduce((s,v,i)=>s+v*y[i],0);\nconst apply=(m,v)=>m.map(row=>dot(row,v));\nconst lmsLab=inv(labLms);\nconst decode=u=>u<=.04045?u/12.92:((u+.055)/1.055)**2.4;\nconst encode=u=>u<=.0031308?12.92*u:1.055*u**(1/2.4)-.055;\nconst clamp=u=>Math.min(1,Math.max(0,u));\nconst pixels=h=>h.slice(1).match(/../g).map(s=>Number.parseInt(s,16));\nconst hex=p=>'\"'#'+p.map(x=>x.toString(16).padStart(2,'0')).join('');\nconst lin=p=>p.map(u=>decode(u/255));\nconst lab=rgb=>apply(lmsLab,apply(xyzLms,apply(rgbXyz,rgb)).map(Math.cbrt));\nconst lch=h=>{const [L,a,b]=lab(lin(pixels(h)));return [L,Math.hypot(a,b),(Math.atan2(b,a)*180/Math.PI+360)%360];};\nconst hue=(a,b)=>Math.abs(((lch(a)[2]-lch(b)[2]+540)%360)-180);\nconst lum=h=>dot(lin(pixels(h)),[.2126,.7152,.0722]);\nconst contrast=(a,b)=>{const l=lum(a)+.05,k=lum(b)+.05;return Math.max(l,k)/Math.min(l,k);};\nconst simulate=(p,v)=>apply(cvd[v],lin(p)).map(clamp);\nconst roundSim=(p,v)=>simulate(p,v).map(c=>Math.round(255*encode(c)));\nconst vision=(p,v,bytes)=>lab(bytes?lin(roundSim(p,v)):simulate(p,v));\nconst delta=(a,b)=>Math.hypot(...a.map((v,i)=>v-b[i]));\nfunction minimum(a,adjacent=false){\n  let min=Infinity,pair=[];\n  for(let i=0;i<a.length;i++)for(let j=i+1;j<(adjacent?i+2:a.length);j++){\n    if(j>=a.length) continue;\n    const z=delta(a[i],a[j]);if(z<min){min=z;pair=[i+1,j+1];}\n  }\n  return {min,pair};\n}\nconst blend=(p,b,k)=>p.map((c,i)=>b[i]+k*(c-b[i]));\nconst rasterModel=(p,b,k,round)=>blend(p,b,round(255*k)/255).map(Math.round);\nconst nround=(num,d=6)=>+num.toFixed(d);\nconst pairText=({min,pair})=>nround(min).toFixed(6)+'('+pair.join('-')+')';\nconst failed=[];\nfunction check(name,a,b,d){\n  const aa=d===undefined?a:nround(a,d);\n  if(JSON.stringify(aa)\"'!==JSON.stringify(b))failed.push([name,aa,b]);\n}\nfunction box(p){const out=[];for(const i of [-1,0,1])for(const j of [-1,0,1])for(const k of [-1,0,1]){\n  const bytes=[i,j,k].map((r,n)=>Math.max(0,Math.min(255,p[n]+r)));\n  out.push(lab(lin(bytes)));\n} return out;}\nconst neighbours=a=>a.slice(1).map((b,i)=>delta(a[i],b));\nconst worst=(a,b)=>Math.min(...box(a).flatMap(x=>box(b).map(y=>delta(x,y))));\nfunction rowsFor(name,series,other,verify=true) {\n  const {background,focus,reference,muted}=specs[name], rec=rom.schemes[name];\n  const ps=series.map(pixels), bg=pixels(background);\n  const cs=series.map(h=>contrast(h,background));\n  const ls=series.map(lch);\n  const hs=series.map((s,i)=>hue(s,other[i]));\n  console.log(name, '\"'L min/max, first3 spread, C max', [Math.min(...ls.map(x=>x[0])),Math.max(...ls.map(x=>x[0])),Math.max(...ls.slice(0,3).map(x=>x[0]))-Math.min(...ls.slice(0,3).map(x=>x[0])),Math.max(...ls.map(x=>x[1]))].map(x=>nround(x)));\n  console.log(name, 'rows [slot, color, L,C,H,contrast,hue shift, focus ratio]',series.map((s,i)=>[i+1,s,...ls[i].map(v=>nround(v)),nround(cs[i]),nround(hs[i]),nround(contrast(s,focus))]));\n  if(verify){\n    check(name+' background',rec.background,background); \n    for(let i=0;i<8;i++){\n      const r=rec.series[i];check(name+' slot',i+1,r.slot);check(name+' hex',series[i],r.hex);check(name+' L',ls[i][0],r.oklch[0],3);check(name+' C',ls[i][1],r.oklch[1],3);check(name+' h',ls[i][2],r.oklch[2],1); check(name+' contrast',cs[i],r.contrast,2);check(name+' hue',hs[i],r.hueDiffToOtherScheme,1);\n    }\n  }\n  for(const n of [3,4,5,6,8]){\n    const rows=visions.map(v=>[false,true].map(by=>{\n      const m=minimum(ps.slice(0,n).map(p=>vision(p,v,by)));\n      if(verify){const r=n===8?rec[by?'minDeltaBytes':'minDelta'][v]:rec[by?'prefixesBytes':'prefixes'][n][v];\n        check(name+n+v+by,m.min,r.min,3);check(name+n+v+by,m.pair,r.pair);}\n      return pairText(m);\n    }).join('/'));\n    console.log(name,n,rows.join(' '));\n  }\n  const token=[REDACTED_SECRET]\n    const dl=lab(lin(pixels(h))), ds=ps.map(p=>delta(lab(lin(p)),dl)), min=Math.min(...ds), slot=ds.indexOf(min)+1;\n    if(verify){check(name+k,min,rec.tokenDistance[k].min,3);check(name+k,slot,rec.tokenDistance[k].slot);}\n    return [k,nround(min),slot,nround(contrast(h,background))];\n  });\n  console.log(name,'tokens',token);\n  for(const a of [.25,.8]){\n    const round=ps.map(p=>rasterModel(p,bg,a,Math.round));\n    const floor=ps.map(p=>rasterModel(p,bg,a,Math.floor));\n    const ideal=ps.map(p=>blend(p,bg,a));\n    const neighbourWorst=round.slice(1).map((p,i)=>worst(round[i],p));\n    const base=[['ideal',ideal],['round',round],['floor',floor]];\n    if(verify){\n      const recFill=rec.raster[a];check(name+' model '+a,round.map(hex),recFill.model);check(name+' floor '+a,floor.map(hex),recFill.modelFloor);\n      const nr=neighbours(round.map(p=>lab(lin(p))));check(name+' model neighbors '+a,nr.map(x=>nround(x,3)),recFill.neighboursModel);check(name+' model minimum '+a,Math.min(...nr),recFill.minModel,3);\n      check(name+' worst neighbors '+a,neighbourWorst.map(x=>nround(x,3)),recFill.neighboursWorstWithinOneByte);check(name+' worst minimum '+a,Math.min(...neighbourWorst),recFill.minWorstWithinOneByte,3);\n      for(const v of visions){\n        const l=ideal.map(p=>vision(p,v,false)), result=minimum(l,true), r=rec.composites[a][v];\n        check(name+a+v,result.min,r.minNeighbour,3);check(name+a+v,result.pair,r.pair);\n        check(name+a+v,neighbours(l).map(x=>nround(x,3)),r.neighbours);\n        for(const closure of r.ringClosures) check(name+a+v+'ring',delta(l[0],l[closure.slots[0]-1]),closure.d,3);\n      }\n      for(const via of ['canvas','svg']){\n        const px=raster.schemes[name].pixels[via][a];\n        base.push([via,px.map(pixels)]);\n        const r=rec.chromeRaster[via][a], ds=neighbours(px.map(p=>lab(lin(pixels(p)))));\n        check(name+via+a,px,r.pixels);check(name+via+a,ds.map(x=>nround(x,3)),r.neighbours);check(name+via+a,Math.min(...ds),r.min,3);\n      }\n    }\n    console.log(name,'fill',a,base.map(([label,c])=>label+' '+pairText(minimum(c.map(p=>lab(lin(p))),true))).join(' '),'worst',nround(Math.min(...neighbourWorst)), 'worst-pair',neighbourWorst.indexOf(Math.min(...neighbourWorst))+1);\n  }\n}\n\nconst png={\\\"light\\\":{\\\"normal\\\":[\\\"#4a94eb\\\",\\\"#e97200\\\",\\\"#136102\\\",\\\"#7314a2\\\",\\\"#bd585e\\\",\\\"#007baa\\\",\\\"#a52265\\\",\\\"#9293a5\\\"],\\\"protan\\\":[\\\"#6d9aef\\\",\\\"#958300\\\",\\\"#645700\\\",\\\"#0046a6\\\",\\\"#6e6b5e\\\",\\\"#647aac\\\",\\\"#3e4a67\\\",\\\"#8f95a6\\\"],\\\"deutan\\\":[\\\"#558be9\\\",\\\"#b29e00\\\",\\\"#5b5111\\\",\\\"#004b9f\\\",\\\"#887f5c\\\",\\\"#4f6da9\\\",\\\"#626262\\\",\\\"#8e94a4\\\"],\\\"tritan\\\":[\\\"#00a8b4\\\",\\\"#ff5661\\\",\\\"#005e51\\\",\\\"#6c3d5f\\\",\\\"#cd495b\\\",\\\"#00878b\\\",\\\"#b30f41\\\",\\\"#8e9699\\\"]},\\\"dark\\\":{\\\"normal\\\":[\\\"#64acfa\\\",\\\"#de7b2e\\\",\\\"#b2e390\\\",\\\"#9149b9\\\",\\\"#c3513d\\\",\\\"#71d8ff\\\",\\\"#f898b5\\\",\\\"#7a7f93\\\"],\\\"protan\\\":[\\\"#8bb0fd\\\",\\\"#988722\\\",\\\"#ead78a\\\",\\\"#1f66bd\\\",\\\"#6f663a\\\",\\\"#c3d4ff\\\",\\\"#a5aab6\\\",\\\"#7a8194\\\"],\\\"deutan\\\":[\\\"#77a1f8\\\",\\\"#b09d2d\\\",\\\"#e2d394\\\",\\\"#406bb6\\\",\\\"#8c7e3a\\\",\\\"#aec5ff\\\",\\\"#bdbbb3\\\",\\\"#787f92\\\"],\\\"tritan\\\":[\\\"#00bec8\\\",\\\"#f3656c\\\",\\\"#b3ddce\\\",\\\"#8c5e7a\\\",\\\"#d6394d\\\",\\\"#00e4e4\\\",\\\"#ff92a2\\\",\\\"#748385\\\"]}};\nfor(const [n,values] of Object.entries(png)) for(const v of visions) values[v].forEach((h,i)=>{\n const m=hex(roundSim(pixels(specs[n].series[i]),v));\n if(m\"'!==h)console.log(n,v,'\"'slot',i+1,'ideal nearest byte',m,'committed PNG',h);\n});\nconst rows=load('strokes').schemes;\nlet max;\nfor(const [s,spec] of Object.entries(rows))for(const row of spec.rows)for(const d of [1,2])for(const k of ['core','weighted'])for(const stat of ['p10','median']){\n const a=row['canvas@'+d][k][stat],b=row['svg@'+d][k][stat],diff=Math.abs(a-b);\n if(\"'!max||diff>max.diff)max={s,color:row.color,d,k,stat,a,b,diff};\n}\nconsole.log('\"'largest canvas-SVG stroke-stat difference',max);\n\nNODE\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
